  "behavior": [
    "Native restoration retains the pre-acquisition snapshot, compares termios fields/control characters/speeds, and skips unchanged settings. Native cleanup scopes SIGTTOU blocking to the calling thread and restores its previous mask.",
    "Headless required stdout writes check insertion and flushing, latch failure, stop with status 1, and suppress secondary stdout records. Descriptor flags and partial records are not replayed.",
    "Line-mode replies attempt later writes after delivery failure, with a sticky status 1 on otherwise successful exit. Cancellation and propagated nonzero errors keep precedence. Keyboard echo remains best effort.",
    "Consumer failures are rethrown before transport retry decisions, after preserving cancellation priority. Secondary stdout serialization and delivery do not replace an existing operation error.",
    "Preallocated writer state retains line separators across partial/newline failures and is shared by notices, ordinary output and replay. Standard stdout/stderr recover their C and C++ stream states.",
    "Human-facing provider errors preserve printable Unicode, LF and TAB while escaping malformed bytes, other C0 controls, DEL/C1 and the existing unsafe Unicode-control set. Raw error data and body/body_base64 structured representations remain unchanged.",
    "Default-sink lifetime checks observe destructor registration with a positive control. Native teardown checks observe endwin before delscreen while the screen is still valid.",
    "Emergency delivery remains best effort without EAGAIN waiting, with one attempt per released notice. Full-path formatting, notice ownership, allocation-free transfer/fallback, replay order, worker quiescence and original cleanup exceptions are preserved."
  ],
